{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PlancherelNormalisation","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PlancherelSnDataGeneral","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SnIsotypicSpechtSplitInstance"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.nuV_top_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.nuV_top_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/SecondMomentKernelVanishes.lean#L143-L159","doc":"**The (TAIL) first instance in closed form, for every `r ≥ 1`**:\n`ν_n = n(n−2)(n−3)·C(2n−4, n−2) / (3·n!)`, `n = r + 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.nuV_top_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.nuV_top_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/SecondMomentKernelVanishes.lean#L123-L141","doc":"**The (TAIL) first instance: `ν_n ≥ 0`, for every `k ≥ 3`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.tiltedMean_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.tiltedMean_zero","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/SecondMomentKernelVanishes.lean#L113-L115","doc":"**`mean_zero`, at every `k`** — `E₂[ω₃] = 0`, where the corpus had `3 ≤ k ≤ 20`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.secondMomentKernel_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.secondMomentKernel_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/SecondMomentKernelVanishes.lean#L92-L107","doc":"**`Σ_{λ⊢k} (f^λ)²·ω₃(λ) = 0`, for every `k`.** No `decide`, no bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.sum_sytDim_sq_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.sum_sytDim_sq_int","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/SecondMomentKernelVanishes.lean#L82-L88","doc":"The Plancherel normalisation in `ℤ`, for the same enumerator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.sum_sytDim_sq_contentSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.sum_sytDim_sq_contentSq","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/SecondMomentKernelVanishes.lean#L70-L80","doc":"**`Σ_{λ⊢k} (f^λ)²·Σ_□ c(□)² = k!·binom(k,2)`**, over `partsOf` / `sytDim` / `contentSq` —\n`PlancherelSnDataGeneral.sum_partition_content_int` reindexed onto the kernel's enumerator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.sytDim_eq_dimHLF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.sytDim_eq_dimHLF","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/SecondMomentKernelVanishes.lean#L61-L66","doc":"The kernel's hook-length dimension and Identity I's are the same function on a sorted parts\nlist. Both are `#SYT`; this composes the two routes to it that the corpus already has. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.contentSq_eq_sumSqContents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SecondMomentKernelVanishes.contentSq_eq_sumSqContents","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/SecondMomentKernelVanishes.lean#L50-L59","doc":"The kernel's content-square sum and Identity I's are the same function. The two definitions are\nwritten identically, but elaborate differently — `contentSq` leaves the inner `List.range` coerced\n`ℕ → ℤ` as a monadic bind, `sumSqContents` annotates the bound variable and maps directly — so they\nare not `rfl`-equal. ","signatureChunk":0}]}